{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameterReal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameterReal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Abs"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.ofSqNeOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.ofSqNeOne","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/GenericParameterReal.lean#L28-L42","doc":"**The bridge: over `ℝ` the hypothesis is free.**  `q ≠ 0` and `q ^ 2 ≠ 1` already give\nit, because the only real roots of unity are `±1` — so every `ℝ`-statement in the\nWedderburn cone is the specialisation of a `NotRootOfUnity` statement, and generalising\nthose files weakens no hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}